    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25807" root="ضرغم" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِرْغَامَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِرْغَامٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Hence, as being likened
to a lion, (TA,) (tropical:)  <i>Courageous;</i> (K, TA;) as an
epithet applied to a man. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And (assumed tropical:)  A
<i>powerful</i> stallion [camel]. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And (tropical:)  A <i>strong</i>
man; (K, TA;) as being likened to a lion. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِرْغَامَةٌ مِنْ طِينٍ</span> is said in the Nawádir
el-Aaráb to mean <i>Slime,</i> or <i>mire.</i> (TA.)

